Z||000000||MARCUS||11-04-2000||07:23 PM||||i bought an 85' fiero gt recently and the decklid on the engine compartment doesn't have a keylock to release it, it looks as tho they fiberglassed over it for a custom look. so i've been releasing it with the electric rocker swith on the dash. the problem is the relay or something has now failed and i can't get into my engine compartment now. anybody with an answer to this would be appreciated. thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-04-2000||07:54 PM||||I'd start by checking the switch, fuse, wiring, etc. inside the car. If you don't find any problems there, you will have to drill a hole in the deck big enough to fit a screwdriver in to turn the latch. You should measure another car to find out where to drill.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
